abstract: |
  RepD3D is a graphical toolbox (Windows executable and Python source) to identify wind-based
  unfiltered and reduced representative periods and to extract the associated boundary
  conditions for coastal modelling studies. A selective-class correlation method identifies
  representative periods for user-defined wind speeds and directions. Version 2 extracts water
  level, currents, waves, salinity, biogeochemistry and Neumann boundary forcing from EasyGSH-DB,
  TrilaWatt, Copernicus Marine and custom NetCDF sources, and wind, pressure and temperature
  fields from COSMO-REA6, ICON-DREAM and ERA5, writing Delft3D-4 and Delft3D FM input files.
